---
description: Basic rules
---

- don't change whitespaces or newlines in the existing unrelated code
- never add whitespaces or tabs to empty lines
- don't remove unrelated code
- don't change files when/where modifications are not needed
- don't add trailing newlines at the end of file, last newline character is at the end of code

## PR atomicity
- each PR must be independently mergeable without breaking the build, tests, or CI
- when removing a feature, pipeline, or task, remove all references (CI config, tests, build scripts, documentation) in a single PR — do not split removals into a deletion PR and a separate cleanup PR, as the intermediate state between merges will break CI
- when a change requires coordinated modifications across multiple files, include all of them in one PR
